        ],
        "type": "object"
      },
      "minItems": 1,
      "type": "array"
    }
  },
  "type": "object"
}

output:
This JSON schema describes an object that represents a configuration for a builder that performs operations on one or multiple sub-builders and targets. The object has two main properties: "builders" and "targets".

- The "builders" property is an array of objects, each representing a sub-builder. Each sub-builder object must have a "builder" property, which is a string that matches any string pattern (i.e., any string), and an "options" property, which is an object containing any additional options for the sub-builder.

- The "targets" property is also an array of objects, each representing a target. Each target object must have a "target" property, which is a string that matches any string pattern (i.e., any string), and an optional "overrides" property, which is an object containing any override options for the target.

Here is a valid example of an object that conforms to this schema:

```
{
  "builders": [
    {
      "builder": "builder1:sub-builder1",
      "options": {
        "option1": "value1",
        "option2": "value2"
      }
    },
    {
      "builder": "builder1:sub-builder2",
      "options": {
        "option3": "value3"
      }
    }
  ],
  "targets": [
    {
      "target": "target1",
      "overrides": {
        "override1": "value4"
      }
    },
    {
      "target": "target2"
    }
  ]
}
```

