output:
This JSON schema describes the structure and format of a "Playbook" object used by the Release Engine. A Playbook is a document that outlines the steps required to successfully start and finish a software release. It defines the actions that the Release Engine will take during a deployment.

A valid Playbook object must have the following properties:

- `execution`: An array of objects that define the hosts, steps, and description of the deployment.
- `name`: A string that gives the name of the Playbook.
- `group`: A string that categorizes the Playbook.

Each object in the `execution` array must have the following properties:

- `hosts`: An array of one or more hostnames or IP addresses that the deployment will target.
- `steps`: An array of one or more step types, which can be either a string (e.g., "task:ACTION") or an object with a step type and optional notify properties.
- `preflight`: An optional array of step types that will be executed before the main deployment steps.
- `description`: A string that describes the purpose and scope of the deployment.

Here is an example of a valid Playbook object:

```json
{
  "execution": [
    {
      "hosts": ["host1", "host2", "host3"],
      "steps": [
        "task:install",
        {
          "task:install": {
            "notify": {
              "started": ["http://example.com/notify"],
              "completed": ["http://example.com/notify"],
              "failed": ["http://example.com/notify"]
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "preflight": ["task:check_dependencies"],
      "description": "Install new software release"
    }
  ],
  "name": "Install Software Release",
  "group": "Deployment"
}
```

