output:
This JSON schema describes a configuration object for obtaining and displaying Markdown-formatted text. It has three main properties: "markdown", "messages" and "i18n".

- The "markdown" property is required and contains information about where to obtain the Markdown-formatted text. It has four possible properties: "parameter", "resource", "attribute" and "url". 
  - "parameter" is a string that represents a place parameter for the flow definition to support anchors.
  - "resource" is either a string representing a topic under which Markdown-formatted text is expected or a URL referencing a file with Markdown-formatted text.
  - "attribute" is a string representing the path to the actual Markdown-formatted text.
  - "url" is a string representing the URL which refers to a Markdown-formatted text.

- The "messages" property is an object that contains configuration for messages published via didEncounterError or didValidate events. It has one property: "i18nFailedLoadingResource", which can be either a string or an object. If it's an object, it contains translations for different locales. The message will be published when a GET for a Markdown-formatted text source fails, and "[url]" will be replaced by the URL.

- The "i18n" property is an object that contains information about the locale to use for displaying the widget. It has one property: "locale", which is a string representing the topic under which to expect the locale for this widget. The default locale is "default".

Here is a valid example of this object:

```json
{
  "markdown": {
    "parameter": "anchor",
    "resource": "com.example.topic",
    "attribute": "text/markdown"
  },
  "messages": {
    "i18nFailedLoadingResource": {
      "en": "Could not load resource from \"[url]\"",
      "de": "Die Ressource konnte nicht von \"[url]\" geladen werden."
    }
  },
  "i18n": {
    "locale": "com.example.locale"
  }
}
```

