**User Token Claim Schema:**
This JSON schema defines the structure and format of a JSON Web Token (JWT) used to authenticate a user with a system. It provides a set of claims that can be included in the token to validate the user's identity and authentication status. The schema allows for two types of user identities: a "sub" claim with a specific format or a "user" object with an "id" and "accountId". The token can also include an "authentication" claim to indicate whether the user is authenticated or unauthenticated, and an "iss" claim to identify the issuer of the token.

**Valid Example:**
```json
{
  "authentication": "authenticated",
  "iss": "https://example.com",
  "sub": "12345:67890@abc:users",
  "user": {
    "id": "67890",
    "accountId": "12345"
  }
}
```
Alternatively, the "sub" claim could be used without the "iss" and "authentication" claims:
```json
{
  "sub": "12345:67890@abc:users",
  "user": {
    "id": "67890",
    "accountId": "12345"
  }
}
```

