The "calendar" section defines the parameter to use for selecting dates. It has a single property "parameter" with a default value of "date".

The "events" section defines which events to display in the calendar. It requires a "resource" property and has an optional "types" array. The "resource" property specifies the name of the events resource to pull events from, and the "types" array specifies the types of events that should be listed (all other events will be ignored).

The "search" section defines how to subscribe to a resource for search queries. It requires a "resource" property and has "fields" and "match" properties. The "resource" property specifies the name of the resource to subscribe to for search queries. The "fields" property is a list of JSON pointers (or paths) pointing to object members to match. The "match" property is a mapping from regular expressions to field lists. The last matching group will be searched in the corresponding object members.

The "details" section defines how to handle details display. It has "resource" and "action" properties. The "resource" property specifies the name of the resource to publish details with, and the "action" property specifies which action to trigger when details shall be displayed.

The "navigation" section provides a resource representing navigation targets. It has "resource" and "interval" properties. The "resource" property specifies the name of the navigation resource, and the "interval" property specifies the interval of navigation (years, months, weeks or days).

